The bug is that `timer` is never assigned, so `clearTimeout(timer)` clears nothing and every keystroke schedules its own call. Store the id:

```javascript
function debounce(fn, wait) {
  let timer;
  return function (...args) {
    clearTimeout(timer);
    timer = setTimeout(() => fn.apply(this, args), wait);
  };
}
```

Now each call cancels the previous pending timeout, so `fn` runs once after the keystrokes stop.

[[GIST]] assign timer to setTimeout

